dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.menu.opt.mastery = Teach me a Focus.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.menu.opt.oath = I want to swear or break an oath.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.menu.opt.focus = What is a Focus?
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.menu.opt.farewell = Farewell.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.about_focus.text = A Focus is one discipline, taken all the way. A weapon, an element, or the Bulwark, for those who stand in front.\nBuy its steps from me with the points your skills earn and some <b>Essence of Life</b>. What you buy, you keep.\nSworn, a Focus makes its weapon or its element hit harder, and its own move is yours to use.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.about_focus.opt.oath = What does an oath cost?
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.about_focus.opt.second = Can I hold more than one?
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.about_oath.text = Swear a Focus here, with me. Swearing costs nothing.\nAn oath takes something while it stands. A weapon oath takes some of your health, an element oath some of your mana, and the Bulwark takes some of the force out of every blow you strike.\nBreak it here and all of that comes back. Breaking costs <b>Essence of Life</b>, so choose with some care.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.about_second.text = You start with room for one oath.\nFinish one Focus, every step of it, and I will set you a task. Do it, and a second oath opens.\nOnly one of your oaths may be a weapon. A weapon with an element, an element with the Bulwark, two elements: those I allow.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.first_oath_offer.text = You can own a Focus and never swear to it. Most people do.\nBuy the Vow of a weapon, an element or the Bulwark from me, then come back and swear it here. A Vow opens once its skill has grown far enough.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.first_oath_offer.opt.accept = I will swear one.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.first_oath_active.text = Buy the Vow of a Focus from me, then swear it here, in front of me.\nNot sure which? Ask me what a Focus is first.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.first_oath_sworn.text = There. Sworn, and you felt it.\nWhile it stands, your Focus counts in every fight. You can break it here if you change your mind, but it will cost you.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.first_oath_sworn.opt.done = It is sworn.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.second_oath_offer.text = Every step of a Focus, bought. Not many get that far.\nI can make room for a second oath. Show me the one you hold is worth it first: take it out into the world and put down <b>foes</b> with it sworn. A foe that falls while you hold no oath does not count. Then come back to me.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.second_oath_offer.opt.accept = I will show you.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.second_oath_active.text = Out you go, and keep your oath sworn. The fighting is done out in the world.\nNothing in this hall will fight you back, so do not bother trying.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.second_oath_ready.text = Back on your own feet. Good.\nCollect what I owe you, and a second oath is yours to swear.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.second_oath_ready.opt.collect = Let me collect it.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.lessons_fresh.text = My board has fresh lessons on it today. Every one of them is done out in the world.\nFinish one and come back here to collect what it pays.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.tithe_credit.text = You sent me a tithe for a long while, and I kept count.\nI teach lessons now, and I pay as you rise. What you already gave counts.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.tithe_credit.opt.collect = What does it count for?
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.first_words.text = So the guide sent you over after all.\nA skill does not stop where its levels do. What comes after is what I teach: a Focus, one weapon or one element taken all the way, and sworn.
dialogue.mmo_mastery_trainer.first_words.opt.hail = The guide spoke of you.
